## 2. APIs Outside @data/api

**Context:** When creating API services. All HTTP calls must be centralized in `src/data/api/`.

**Forbidden:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: API service in presentation
// src/presentation/services/vagaService.ts
export const vagaService = {
  async buscarVagas() {
    const response = await fetch('/api/vagas'); // Direct fetch!
    return response.json();
  }
};

// ❌ BAD: API service in shared
// src/shared/api/usuarioApi.ts
export const buscarUsuario = async (id: string) => {
  const response = await axios.get(`/api/usuarios/${id}`); // Direct axios!
  return response.data;
};

// ❌ BAD: Inline API calls in components
// src/presentation/pages/Perfil.tsx
useEffect(() => {
  fetch('/api/perfil') // Direct fetch in component!
    .then(r => r.json())
    .then(setPerfil);
}, []);
```

**Required:**

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: All APIs centralized in @data/api
// src/data/api/VagaApi.ts
import { createHttpClient } from './httpClient';
import type { ApiResponse } from '@/shared/types/api';

export interface VagaResponse {
  id: string;
  titulo: string;
  descricao: string;
}

export const vagaApi = {
  async listar(): Promise<ApiResponse<VagaResponse[]>> {
    const httpClient = createHttpClient();
    return httpClient.get('/api/Vaga/Listar');
  },
  
  async obterPorId(id: string): Promise<ApiResponse<VagaResponse>> {
    const httpClient = createHttpClient();
    return httpClient.get(`/api/Vaga/Obter/${id}`);
  },
  
  async criar(dados: CriarVagaRequest): Promise<ApiResponse<VagaResponse>> {
    const httpClient = createHttpClient();
    return httpClient.post('/api/Vaga/Criar', dados);
  }
};

// ✅ GOOD: Presentation uses repository, not API directly
// src/presentation/pages/Perfil.tsx
const PerfilPage = () => {
  const container = useContainer();
  const obterPerfilUseCase = container.resolve(ObterPerfilUseCase);
  
  useEffect(() => {
    obterPerfilUseCase.execute().then(setPerfil);
  }, [obterPerfilUseCase]);
};
```

**Structure:**

```
src/
└── data/
    └── api/
        ├── httpClient.ts          # Centralized HTTP client factory
        ├── errorHandler.ts        # Centralized error handling
        ├── VagaApi.ts             # Vaga resource API
        ├── CandidaturaApi.ts      # Candidatura resource API
        ├── UsuarioApi.ts          # Usuario resource API
        └── index.ts               # Re-exports
```

**Impact:**

- Lack of standardization - different APIs do things differently
- Multiple change points - fix auth, fix in N files
- Inconsistent error handling - some APIs handle errors differently
- Harder to add cross-cutting concerns (logging, auth, retries)

**Detection:**

- `fetch(` or `axios` outside of `src/data/api/`
- Check: `grep -r "fetch\|axios" src/presentation/ src/shared/` (should be empty)
- API-related files outside `data/api` folder
- Direct HTTP calls in components or hooks

**Architecture Reference:**

See `@ARCHITECTURE.md` Section 5: "APIs em `@data/api` (CandidaturaApi, VagaApi, etc.) centralizam as requisicoes. Nao usar fetch/axios diretamente."

See `@DESIGN_SYSTEM_AUDIT.md` Section 1.2: "APIs usando httpClient (nao fetch() direto)."

